# Build context for the app image (Dockerfile does `COPY . .`).
#
# Without this file every secret in the repo directory was baked into the
# image layers: .env.production, the Cloudflare origin TLS private key, and
# the full .git history. None of them were web-reachable (nginx only
# proxy_passes; Werkzeug blocks /static traversal), but anyone holding the
# image — `docker save`, a registry push, a container escape — held them all.
#
# Nothing below is needed inside the app image:
#   - env vars arrive at runtime via compose `env_file: .env.production`
#   - nginx reads its certs through its own bind mount, not this image
#   - the build SHA arrives as the GIT_SHA build arg (ship.sh), not via .git

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
nginx/certs/
*.key
*.pem
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# ── VCS and tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.claude/
cowork_*_prompt.md

# ── Local-only and generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
exports/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
